  "id": "improvisation",
  "term": "improvisation",
  "definition": "Improvisation is the real-time creation of action by drawing on learned, embodied patterns rather than acting with complete freedom or simply repeating fixed routines. In psychology of learning, it can be understood as a structured, culturally shaped process in which people reorganize kinesthetic and procedural memories in response to shared cues and current demands.",
